From: Jaime Dias <jaimejosediasnt@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 12:20:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 12/22] m68k-all: define cpumask_t, as every other arch does

arm, aarch64, riscv and riscv64 typedef it to unsigned int; i386 and
x86_64 to void *. m68k defined it nowhere, so any generic code carrying a
cpumask_t field failed to compile for this architecture -- found while
building the BCM2708 USB OTG driver, whose unit structure has one.
---
 arch/m68k-all/include/aros/cpu.h | 8 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/m68k-all/include/aros/cpu.h b/arch/m68k-all/include/aros/cpu.h
index 97c5bf5a88..31be6b6a83 100644
--- a/arch/m68k-all/include/aros/cpu.h
+++ b/arch/m68k-all/include/aros/cpu.h
@@ -27,6 +27,16 @@
 
 #define AROS_SLOWSTACKFORMAT 1
 
+/*
+    A set of CPUs, as a bitmask.
+
+    Every other maintained architecture defines this -- arm, aarch64, riscv and
+    riscv64 as unsigned int, i386 and x86_64 as void * -- and m68k defined it
+    nowhere, so generic code carrying a cpumask_t field simply did not compile
+    for this architecture.
+*/
+typedef unsigned int    cpumask_t;
+
 #define AROS_NOFPU 1
 
 /* do we need a function attribute to get parameters on the stack? */
